# Build context for docker/k3-split-prefill/k3-split-prefill.Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore in preference to the context
# root's .dockerignore, so this file governs THIS build only and leaves the
# repo's root .dockerignore (a symlink to .gitignore) alone.
#
# The context is the repo root, and the image only needs source. Everything
# excluded here is either regenerable, a run output, or host-specific.

# 309 MB of history the image cannot use. setuptools_scm falls back to
# 0.0.0.dev0 without it; provenance is carried by the SGLANG_BUILD_COMMIT
# build-arg instead (see the Dockerfile header), which is cheaper and pins the
# sha into a label you can read off a running container.
.git

# Run outputs. runs/ is ~103 MB and grows; edr/*.pt dumps are 333 MB each.
# These belong on the host and are mounted at /workspace/runs at run time.
runs/

# Local tooling and caches
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Build artifacts that must be rebuilt inside the image, never copied in --
# a host-built .so links against the host's torch/CUDA and breaks the image.
**/*.so
**/*.o
**/*.a
build/
dist/
**/*.egg-info/
python/sglang/_version.py
rust/target/
sgl-model-gateway/target/
sgl-kernel/build/

# Not consumed by this image
docs/
benchmark/
examples/
assets/
prof*/
